Facility Capacity Reservation is part of Data Center Control Plane (DCCP),
Tranche 2: Facility Capacity and Placement. It is repository 15 of the canonical
72-runtime DCCP and owns facility-capacity commitments across space, rack, power,
cooling and explicit facility services: reservation identity and generations,
typed multi-resource claims, exact source-generation preconditions, headroom
accounting, validity intervals, lifecycle, amendment lineage, idempotent retry,
durable crash-safe publication and reconciliation against newly consumed capacity
snapshots.

Facility Capacity Reservation sits above Accelerated Systems Infrastructure (ASI)
and Distributed Fabric Infrastructure (DFI). It does not own accelerator
execution, memory, serving or scheduling (ASI), network topology, paths,
transport or bandwidth (DFI), the derivation of facility capacity (Facility
Capacity and the source capacity runtimes), placement selection (Facility
Placement Planner), or rack, asset, power and cooling actuation (Rack Registry,
Asset Registry, Power Control, Cooling Control).

Third-party notices
------------------

This product includes no third-party source code and links no third-party
libraries. It is implemented against the C++20 standard library and the
operating-system interfaces it needs for durable atomic file replacement and
advisory inter-process file locking.

The canonical serialization format, the integrity digest (SHA-256, FIPS 180-4)
and every identity, generation, epoch and attempt type are implemented in this
repository.
